WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:21.427 --> 00:00:25.016
- I think everybody thinks
that 2012 was a fluke,

00:00:25.016 --> 00:00:27.516
like I got lucky or something.

00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:32.889
I'm the first black, white, whatever,

00:00:32.889 --> 00:00:35.354
the first woman to win an
Olympic gold medal in boxing

00:00:35.354 --> 00:00:37.736
and I did it when I was 17.

00:00:37.736 --> 00:00:40.475
I thought I would have
endorsements and sponsorships,

00:00:40.475 --> 00:00:42.392
but, you know, that didn't happen.

00:00:45.272 --> 00:00:48.111
- Welcome back everybody,
thank you so much.

00:00:48.111 --> 00:00:49.633
My guest tonight—

00:00:49.633 --> 00:00:51.058
- I am the best female boxer in the world.

00:00:51.058 --> 00:00:52.225
- Grew up in Flint, Michigan—

00:00:52.225 --> 00:00:54.989
- They’d be like you know,
when you talk you seem

00:00:54.989 --> 00:00:56.434
like a bully or you seem pretty cocky.

00:00:56.434 --> 00:00:58.856
If you want us to do your
hair we'll do your hair.

00:00:58.856 --> 00:00:59.689
And I was like, what's wrong with my hair?

00:00:59.689 --> 00:01:01.299
So I can't express how
great of a fighter I am.

00:01:01.299 --> 00:01:02.778
Okay, they want the pretty girl.

00:01:02.778 --> 00:01:03.804
I back up everything I say.

00:01:03.804 --> 00:01:07.600
Nothing is wrong with my personality.

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:09.980
Maybe this is the peak of my career.

00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:12.111
Maybe 17 was it.

00:01:12.111 --> 00:01:16.278
Maybe one Olympic gold medal
and better start having kids now.

00:01:22.337 --> 00:01:25.009
- [Radio] Comes alive,
experience over 40 life-size

00:01:25.009 --> 00:01:27.852
moving, breathing dinosaurs
in their natural environment.

00:01:27.852 --> 00:01:31.303
See the amazing 20-foot T-Rex,
the life-size triceratops,

00:01:31.303 --> 00:01:32.303
stegosaurus.

00:01:35.617 --> 00:01:36.450
- Are you getting in the car?

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:37.283
- [Voiceover] Huh?

00:01:37.283 --> 00:01:38.251
- Getting in the car?

00:01:38.251 --> 00:01:39.084
- [Voiceover] Huh?

00:01:39.084 --> 00:01:39.939
- Getting in?

00:01:39.939 --> 00:01:40.772
- [Voiceover] Yeah.

00:01:40.772 --> 00:01:42.522
- All right, come on.

00:01:43.873 --> 00:01:47.928
♫ Going on across the sea ♫

00:01:47.928 --> 00:01:51.678
(music and talking on radio)

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:08.281
- [Claressa] People in
Flint are so used to just

00:02:08.281 --> 00:02:12.198
somebody being successful
and then falling off.

00:02:14.833 --> 00:02:16.250
Flint has limits.

00:02:17.672 --> 00:02:19.318
Nobody wants to get in the sky and see

00:02:19.318 --> 00:02:22.318
what's beyond the clouds type thing.

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:27.359
I think for some people
that they get start caring.

00:02:27.359 --> 00:02:28.674
They don't get out the B.S.

00:02:28.674 --> 00:02:31.424
because they kind of get used to it

00:02:32.976 --> 00:02:35.809
and they see no other way of life.

00:02:43.468 --> 00:02:45.947
I cover Mama end of the bargain with you.

00:02:45.947 --> 00:02:47.465
I just went and took you school shopping

00:02:47.465 --> 00:02:49.160
and got you two pair of shoes, bro.

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:52.704
I keep telling you go to school,
play football, run track.

00:02:52.704 --> 00:02:53.572
- You don't know shit.

00:02:53.572 --> 00:02:54.878
(unclear)

00:02:54.878 --> 00:02:56.123
- Makeel went to the camera,
Ilikia went to the camera...

00:02:56.123 --> 00:02:58.101
- No, are you going to
go to school or not?

00:02:58.101 --> 00:02:59.046
That's my question for you.

00:02:59.046 --> 00:03:02.087
11:27, bro, are you
going to school or not?

00:03:02.087 --> 00:03:03.866
Decide your own life.

00:03:03.866 --> 00:03:05.476
You're going to sacrifice
your education for her

00:03:05.476 --> 00:03:06.800
'cause you think you know everything.

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:08.387
I said go to school, dumbass.

00:03:08.387 --> 00:03:09.542
I'm-a talk to you later,
bro, because you're

00:03:09.542 --> 00:03:10.875
gonna make me mad and I
don't want to get there.

00:03:10.875 --> 00:03:12.626
- No, your ass gonna make me mad.

00:03:12.626 --> 00:03:14.517
- And what you gonna do about it?

00:03:14.517 --> 00:03:16.600
(sirens)

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:22.336
I know that my family
wants to see me do well.

00:03:22.336 --> 00:03:23.903
But they don't know that some
of the things that they do

00:03:23.903 --> 00:03:25.820
can hurt me doing well.

00:03:32.299 --> 00:03:34.286
You know, we always had a
deal, even when I was younger,

00:03:34.286 --> 00:03:36.548
once you step into the
gym all outside problems

00:03:36.548 --> 00:03:38.798
stay out the gym, you know?

00:03:40.161 --> 00:03:44.244
Felt like I have everything
to lose, 'cause I do.

00:03:51.169 --> 00:03:53.336
(humming)

00:03:56.516 --> 00:03:59.103
I feel like the longer I'm
here the further I drift away.

00:03:59.103 --> 00:04:01.353
Drift back into being here.

00:04:03.454 --> 00:04:06.785
I really, you know, don't just want
to walk out on them,

00:04:06.785 --> 00:04:11.558
but I've always kept my
career first before anything.

00:04:11.558 --> 00:04:13.405
So that's why I'm like the longer I stay

00:04:13.405 --> 00:04:16.988
the worse it is for
me, so it's time to go.

00:04:19.351 --> 00:04:21.518
(dinging)

00:04:22.518 --> 00:04:24.601
I’m-a hit you up, though.

00:04:29.642 --> 00:04:31.392
I love you too, baby.

00:04:44.925 --> 00:04:47.138
I have nothing but time to think.

00:04:47.138 --> 00:04:48.757
Nothing but time to look out the window,

00:04:48.757 --> 00:04:52.840
wonder about what I'm-a
do 15, 20 years from now.

00:04:55.309 --> 00:04:59.226
I have to win to go back
to the Olympics again.

00:05:00.918 --> 00:05:04.917
If I don't win the Olympic
trials, there is no Olympics,

00:05:04.917 --> 00:05:07.917
there is no more USA Boxing stipend.

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:12.113
Will I have to move back to Flint?

00:05:14.218 --> 00:05:18.700
I do believe that I can win
another Olympic gold medal.

00:05:18.700 --> 00:05:23.360
But just because I believe it
don't mean it's gonna happen.

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:25.571
- [Voiceover] Good evening
ladies and gentlemen

00:05:25.571 --> 00:05:29.106
and welcome to the Olympic
team trials for women's boxing.

00:05:29.106 --> 00:05:32.453
Here in ring number one
in Memphis, Tennessee,

00:05:32.453 --> 00:05:36.846
these are the best 24
female boxers in the nation

00:05:36.846 --> 00:05:39.311
competing for the chance
to go to Rio de Janeiro

00:05:39.311 --> 00:05:41.561
for the 2016 Olympic Games.

00:05:42.988 --> 00:05:46.290
(applause and whistling)

00:05:46.290 --> 00:05:49.850
- [Voiceover] Women's
middleweight winners bracket.

00:05:49.850 --> 00:05:52.675
Claressa Shields in the red
corner from Flint, Michigan

00:05:52.675 --> 00:05:56.842
against Tika Hemingway in the
blue corner from Pennsylvania.

00:05:58.721 --> 00:06:00.350
- I can't afford to have a bad fight

00:06:00.350 --> 00:06:02.193
or have a close fight anymore.

00:06:02.193 --> 00:06:05.699
They're gonna be a lot harder
on me now that I’m, you know, top dog.

00:06:05.699 --> 00:06:08.532
And it's either dominate or don't.

00:06:10.036 --> 00:06:11.794
- [Voiceover] She understands
this time around

00:06:11.794 --> 00:06:14.697
that it's much more than
just about winning gold.

00:06:14.697 --> 00:06:18.864
That her image, that her personality
play a much bigger role.

00:06:22.250 --> 00:06:24.615
- People said that when you
talk you seem like a bully

00:06:24.615 --> 00:06:26.698
or you seem pretty cocky.

00:06:29.799 --> 00:06:33.966
I don't have to change myself
for people to accept me.

00:06:35.671 --> 00:06:39.136
I don't care what nobody thinks.

00:06:39.136 --> 00:06:40.088
(bell rings)

00:06:40.088 --> 00:06:43.088
(yelling, groaning)

00:07:01.595 --> 00:07:03.806
- [Voiceover] Right now, right now.

00:07:03.806 --> 00:07:06.590
- [Voiceover] She's hurt.

00:07:06.590 --> 00:07:09.584
(yelling)

00:07:09.584 --> 00:07:11.834
(groaning)

00:07:13.835 --> 00:07:17.002
(many people yelling)

00:07:36.863 --> 00:07:38.249
- [Claressa] If you look
up the word beautiful woman

00:07:38.249 --> 00:07:40.783
in the dictionary it should
have my face right there.

00:07:40.783 --> 00:07:42.824
It should have me in a boxing uniform

00:07:42.824 --> 00:07:45.729
with my gloves on posing.

00:07:45.729 --> 00:07:48.925
To box the way that I
do, that's what I think

00:07:48.925 --> 00:07:50.592
is really beautiful.

00:07:54.475 --> 00:07:57.305
(groaning, people yelling)

00:07:57.305 --> 00:07:59.722
(bell rings)

00:08:00.869 --> 00:08:05.137
- And now your winner
of the women's 165-pound

00:08:05.137 --> 00:08:09.597
weight class, fighting
out of the red corner...

00:08:09.597 --> 00:08:11.990
(cheering and applause)

00:08:11.990 --> 00:08:13.407
Claressa Shields.

00:08:19.220 --> 00:08:21.170
- [Claressa] I think
everybody thinks that 2012

00:08:21.170 --> 00:08:24.753
was a fluke, like I
got lucky or something.

00:08:27.813 --> 00:08:28.646
Eh, okay.

00:08:32.074 --> 00:08:34.163
They can't think that now.

00:08:34.163 --> 00:08:37.830
(upbeat instrumental music)

